{"severity":"error","file":"errors/role_grant_exceeded_2.march","start_line":39,"start_col":82,"end_line":39,"end_col":86,"message":"Role `Stream.Cons` is granted `Cap(IO.NetConnect)` (`role Cons needs IO.NetConnect`), but the body passed to `Stream_Run.run_Cons` reaches `IO.FileWrite` (reached from the body: body → wipe). A role's grant bounds everything its code reaches, as `main`'s grant bounds the program.\nhelp: add `IO.FileWrite` to the grant in protocol `Stream`: `role Cons needs IO.NetConnect, IO.FileWrite`. The body then takes one `Cap` per granted capability, in the grant's order, between the session capability and the state, so it gains a parameter: `fn (s, cap_net_connect, cap_file_write, st) -> ...`. Pass `cap_file_write` on to any function the body hands its capabilities to. Or remove the use.","code":"role_grant_exceeded","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
